the Asia Pacific, the Americas, and Europe. It operates in two segments, Core nutritional and Hiya Direct-To-Consumer. The company offers USANA nutritional optimizers, including supplements for cardiovascular health, skeletal/structural health, and digestive health; Essentials/CellSentials, such as vitamin and mineral supplements for age group beginning with children 13 months of age; and food products that include meal replacement shakes, snack bars, and other related products for healthy weight management, digestive health, and energy and hydration. It offers Celavive, a skincare regimen for various skin care types and ethnicities; and all other products comprising materials and online tools for associates to build business and marketing of products The company sells its products through retail customers, a subscription model, and direct selling, as well as online. The company was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin G. Guest | CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $589K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["USANA Health Sciences, Inc. is a micro-cap consumer defensive business with a $245M market cap on $925M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 50% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 41-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 82% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 44\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 11.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 41% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against 