e would suggest (0.50x).","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-29.2% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.07 across 172 companies in the universe; the top four hold 38% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a steep downtrend, down 20% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the bottom of its 52-week range, 44% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 53% and a beta of 0.75, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.03 vs 5y 0.64), so read it loosely.","About $2.8M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 45% in the 2020 crash, 53% in the 2022 bear market and 62% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 50% below its DCF fair value of $26.47, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 55%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $20.53 to $35.31 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","Multiples send mixed signals against Consumer Defensive peers: cheaper on P/E 10.6 vs 18.3 and EV/EBITDA 1.4 vs 10.2, richer on P/FCF 28.7 vs 16.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 33% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 3.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 37.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The Street target $22.00 on average, 66% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 50% clears the cost of capital of 8.5% by 41pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.46).","It runs a 82% gross margin and converts 1% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.08x.","ROE of 2% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.2% of revenue on R&D and 1.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $158.4M (65% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.5, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.24)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -6.6% over 3 years, -4.0% over 5 years and 0.1% over 10 years, so the decline is deepening.","At current returns, reinvesting 8% of profits supports about 4.1% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -43.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 12%.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (1.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is -5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 40.9%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 59%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (8 sales, net $544K sold).","It returns 11.2% a year to shareholders (11.2% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 1,570 employees, each generates about $589K of revenue, 1.2x the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has grown 3.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $5K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.0M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $9K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":76,"head":"Invest: trades 50% below fair value of $26.47; ROIC 49.8% vs WACC 8.5%.","pros":["Composite 52, above the 39 line (gates 15/26)","Trades 50% below fair value of $26.47","ROIC 49.8% vs WACC 8.5%","Net cash of $158.4M","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Revenue shrank 4.0%/yr over 5y","P/FCF 28.7x vs sector 16.1x","12-1 month momentum -20%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":22.5,"vc":{"base":26.47,"base_src":"dcf","bear":20.53,"bull":35.31,"alt_median":58.55,"n_alt":2,"gap":-0.5479,"dispersion":0.5523,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (55% dispersion)","DCF is 55% below the other models' median ($58.55)"]},"